# Cyclone DDS 0.10.2 SEDP publication announcement (1200 byte datagram)
# Captured on llvm (Debian 6.1) 2026-04-19 via tcpdump on lo0,
# Cyclone-Domain 42, two ddsperf processes (pub + sub).
#
# Datagram structure:
#   - RTPS Header (20 bytes): magic + version 2.1 + vendor 01:10 (Cyclone)
#     + sender GuidPrefix
#   - INFO_DST submessage (id 0x0e, octets 0x0c): target GuidPrefix
#   - INFO_TS submessage (id 0x09, octets 0x08): source timestamp
#   - DATA submessage (id 0x15, flags 0x05=E+D, octets 0x0118=280):
#       readerId 0x000003c7 (SEDP_BUILTIN_PUBLICATIONS_READER)
#       writerId 0x000003c2 (SEDP_BUILTIN_PUBLICATIONS_WRITER)
#       writerSN = 1, encapsulation = 0x0003 (PL_CDR_LE)
#       ParameterList: PID_TOPIC_NAME="DDSPerfCPUStats",
#                     PID_TYPE_NAME="CPUStats",
#                     plus DATA_REPRESENTATION, TYPE_INFORMATION,
#                     RELIABILITY, etc. — closed with PID_SENTINEL
#   - subsequent DATA submessages: additional publications announced
#     in the same datagram (DDSPerfRPingKS, DDSPerfRDataKS,
#     DDSPerfRPongKS), same writerId
#
# Note: the concrete GuidPrefix + endpoint_guid + timestamp values
# are per-run — tests should check structure, not exact bytes for
# those. Topic names and wire layout are deterministic.

